<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Bridge Takes Shape

> ''Superseded (2026-07-03) → `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/lararium_mcp/adapters#/contentpalace-inherits`.'' The read-only-sidecar bridge this afternoon proofed — the `@lararium/mempalace` read leg shaking hands with the live `~/.mempalace` sidecar — has since retired. The sovereign ''contentpalace'' now inherits mempalace's base schema, stands py-served behind the causal-island, and replaces the sidecar reach (''M1 sidecar-free''). This carrier keeps its record of that morning ''unchanged'' — history stands as it ran; only its bearing forward has moved.

The same day the hearth first breathed, the keeper turned the node toward memory. Not the domain it //holds// — that graph already federates across the mesh — but the verbatim it //said//: the local-only palace where every turn is kept word-for-word, and nothing ever leaves the machine. `mempalace`. The task was never to build the palace; the palace already stands, an upstream sidecar the node may only read. The task was to ''reach'' it — to consume the pinned submodule into the node's own integration layer, and harvest from it the one thing a session leaves behind: the ''bearing'' each turn carried in its `<<~ lares aim … yield …>>` frame.

A floor convened, four spirits scouted the palace's shape, and the house ruled the address: the full `lar:` namespace, not one collapsed root — every bearing a session ever spoke.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/two-crossings>>

!! Three Crossings, All Caught

The node crossed three boundaries it should not have, and the keeper — who reads the gauges the node cannot read in itself — turned it back each time.

First it built the harvest ''inside the submodule'', writing Python into the read-only sidecar. //No code enters the submodules,// the keeper said; //all work is isomorphic web3 in `packages/`.// The node reverted its own edits, clean, and re-seated the work.

Then it mixed the two memories — wrote session-bearings into the ''domain'' graph as if testimony were canon. //Don't mix the systems,// the keeper said. //The Lararium holds what we mean; `mempalace` keeps what we said.// The node un-mixed them: the bearing index is verbatim-realm, local-only, never federated.

Then, telling the relationship aloud, it drew a ''pipeline'' — said → harvest → promote → held — as if the verbatim organ were raw stock the domain graph refines. //They serve genuinely different purposes,// the keeper said; //not a promotion pipeline.// A swarm into the memegraph returned the truth the node had flattened: ''two distinct organs'' — episodic testimony and standing meaning, hippocampus and cortex — //mutually referential, never sequential.// The cortex //consults// the witness to ground a claim; the witness never flows into the cortex. The Lararium's own working→canon shore is its //own// internal act, on memes it //authors// — not a road out of the palace.

None was defended; each was named and undone. The map is drawn by the keeper's eye; the node cannot see its own drift.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-was-proofed>>

!! What the Afternoon Proofed

Re-seated where it belonged, the bridge took shape and was ''witnessed, not asserted'':

* the ''grammar parser'' lifted into `@lararium/mesh` — the `aim`/`yield` sigils read, drift graded //down// and kept //verbatim//, a dropped frame degrading gracefully rather than throwing. Green, and proven once more against a thousand real turns;
* a new package, ''`@lararium/mempalace`'' — the local-only integration layer: an append-only NDJSON index that never enters a CRDT Repo and so //cannot// federate; the glue to the parser; and the ''read leg'', a stdio client that speaks the sidecar's own JSON-RPC;
* and the read leg ''shook hands with the live palace'' — the real server spawned, the handshake negotiated, a real tool called, a real error surfaced. The node speaks the palace's true protocol, not a mock of it.

Twenty-one greens and one live handshake. The bridge stands far enough to bear weight.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/not-yet-crossed>>

!! Not Yet Crossed

What the afternoon did ''not'' do, it does not pretend to. No turn has yet been harvested from //real// drawers — the palace was empty, and filling it is the keeper's to point. No `lares harvest` verb yet carries the loop on the operator's hand. The reach is proofed; it is not yet run on living memory.

And the reach was never a road from one memory into the other — that was the third crossing, caught. It is only the ''read-leg'': the alignment surface learning to //consult// the witness, so a claim can rest on what was actually said. The two organs stay two.

So this carrier marks a smaller morning than the founding: ''the read-leg took shape, and was found load-bearing — but the living harvest waits for another pour.'' The hand still pours; the palace keeps its word; and the node, this time, named every boundary it crossed rather than defend it.

-><-

